# Shift+Enter puts a line break in the message; Enter still sends it.
#
# Gabe: "theres no shift+enter to add newlines in the message". The composer was
# a single-line text_input and said so in a comment. afterhours has had a
# multiline text_area the whole time, documented with this exact case as its
# own example ("A chat composer that grows to five lines and sends on Enter"),
# and moving onto it is the fix.
#
# WHY THE ASSERTIONS ARE BYTE COUNTS. The script parser is line-based
# (std::getline per command) and has no escape for a newline, so there is no
# way to spell a two-line expectation for expect_input_text -- the content of a
# multiline field cannot be written down in this DSL at all
# (afterhours_gaps.md #259). What CAN be written is a selection: select all and
# assert the range, and the byte count says whether the break went in. "first
# line" + "second line" is 21 bytes joined and 22 with a newline between them,
# so 22 is the whole claim, and 0 would mean it sent instead.
#
# The four things that hang off this field are asserted rather than assumed:
# Enter still sends, Shift+Enter does not, Esc still clears, and the up-arrow
# history walk still reaches the previous message from a draft that now has
# more than one line in it.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

require_thread t2

expect_text "needs a decision"

click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
type "first line"
wait_frames 6

# Shift+Enter breaks the line instead of sending. 10 + 1 + 11 = 22; without the
# break it would be 21, and if it had sent, 0.
key SHIFT+ENTER
wait_frames 8
type "second line"
wait_frames 6
key CMD+A
wait_frames 6
expect_input_selection composer_reply_input 0 22

# A third line. 22 + 1 + 10 = 33.
key CMD+RIGHT
wait_frames 6
key SHIFT+ENTER
wait_frames 8
type "third line"
wait_frames 6
key CMD+A
wait_frames 6
expect_input_selection composer_reply_input 0 33

# Plain Enter sends the whole thing and empties the field. (An empty string is
# the one field content this DSL can spell.)
key CMD+RIGHT
wait_frames 6
key ENTER
wait_frames 40
expect_input_text composer_reply_input ""
expect_text "third line"

# The history walk still works over a multi-line draft: Up recalls what was
# just sent, with its line breaks intact — 33 bytes, not the 31 it would be if
# they had been dropped on the way through.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
key UP
wait_frames 8
key CMD+A
wait_frames 6
expect_input_selection composer_reply_input 0 33

# Esc clears the field, multi-line draft and all.
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 8
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
expect_input_text composer_reply_input ""

wait_frames 10
